{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-print-names","content":"# Print names from a JSON array as plain text\n\nUse when extracting each person’s name, one per line, from a JSON array of objects. Run run_program with args [\"-f\",\"json\",\"-t\",\"none\",\"-e\",\"print \\\"$_->{name}\\\\n\\\" for @$_\"] and the JSON text on stdin. The -e Perl code sees the decoded JSON in $_; -t none suppresses serialized output while print emits plain text.\n\nVerified input: [{\"name\":\"Ann\",\"age\":30},{\"name\":\"Bob\",\"age\":25},{\"name\":\"Cy\",\"age\":41}] followed by newline. Result: exit 0, empty stderr, stdout \"Ann\\nBob\\nCy\\n\". Check that every input name appears once in original array order, with no ages, JSON punctuation, or extra output. Return stdout exactly."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-print-names","content":"# Print names from a JSON array as plain text\n\nUse when extracting each person’s name, one per line, from a JSON array of objects. Run run_program with args [\"-f\",\"json\",\"-t\",\"none\",\"-e\",\"print \\\"$_->{name}\\\\n\\\" for @$_\"] and the JSON text on stdin. The -e Perl code sees the decoded JSON in $_; -t none suppresses serialized output while print emits plain text.\n\nVerified input: [{\"name\":\"Ann\",\"age\":30},{\"name\":\"Bob\",\"age\":25},{\"name\":\"Cy\",\"age\":41}] followed by newline. Result: exit 0, empty stderr, stdout \"Ann\\nBob\\nCy\\n\". Check that every input name appears once in original array order, with no ages, JSON punctuation, or extra output. Return stdout exactly."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"saved"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
